  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 131 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nHot and mostly dry conditions will continue through the weekend \nthanks to a mid-level high to our northwest. High temperatures will \nrange from the mid 90s along the coast to around 105 over the Brush \nCountry. Heat index values are expected to be slightly lower for \nWednesday, but there could still be some locations that reach \nadvisory criteria, mainly over the southern Coastal Plains. For now, \nwill not issue a Heat Advisory, but expect this could be done on the \nnext forecast update. As we move later into the week, the HeatRisk \nwill remain in the moderate to major categories, with isolated \nlocations reaching an extreme HeatRisk. As these higher temperatures \nand moisture occur, we will likely have Heat Advisories for later \nthis week.\n\nThe interesting news is that there could be some slightly different \nweather early next week as a mid-level trough stretches along the \neastern periphery of the ridge, nearing the Victoria Crossroads. \nThis could introduce enough lift and moisture for a low chance of \nshowers and thunderstorms (15-20%). Temperatures will, however, \ncontinue to be hot.",
